<title>TURKEY: Turkish Isbank 1996 H1 net proift jumps.</title>
<headline>Turkish Isbank 1996 H1 net proift jumps.</headline>
<text>
<p>ISTANBUL, Aug 26 (Reuter) 1996 first half final (billion lira unless stated)</p>
<p>    Per share profit (lira)     914.84   vs    2,022.22</p>
<p>    Net profit		    9,148.38   vs    5,055.55</p>
<p>    Net interest income	30,661.56   vs   11,836.72</p>
<p>    Net non-interest expense 45,319.79   vs   18,357.77</p>
<p>    Provisions for bad loans    666.93   vs	433.21</p>
<p>    Deposits		    325,363.96   vs  172,959.28</p>
<p>    Loans borrowed	     25,036.92   vs   25,582.38</p>
<p>    Equity			 51,272.19   vs   23,969.08</p>
<p>    Capital			10,000.00   vs    2,500.00</p>
<p>NOTE - Turkiye Isbankasi A.S., one of Turkey's biggest commercial banks, operates with 825 domestic branches, one in London and three in the Turkish Republic of northern Cyrpus.</p>
<p>Is Bank is owned 44.4 percent by the bank's pension fund and 39.4 percent by the Turkish Treasury.</p>
<p>The figures above do not take into account Turkey's 82.9 percent year-on-year consumer price inflation in June.</p>
<p>-- Istanbul Newsroom, +90-212-275 0875 SA</p>
</text>
